      say: `Two outputs carry the chapter's end date. The island list holds every account that will stay on Kerberos, under the name it will end up with, along with its owner, its end date, and whether it's ready to hand to the program's retirement work. The hand-off flag only turns true when every single row is ready. The reconciliation covers every managed account, existing or planned, and says where it ends up. When the program confirms its end-state decision, that file changes in a reviewed pull request and the run is repeated well before A D retires.`,
      detail: `island-list.csv holds every account that stays on Kerberos under the name it will have (the dMSA or gMSA a conversion creates, or the account itself), with its SPNs, SPN owner, end date, whether the date is within D08 and whether it is ready for the program's SPN retirement (P4.6). The run's manifest records islandHandoffReady, true only when D08 is set and every row is ready. reconciliation.json holds every gMSA and dMSA, existing or planned, with its destination and outcome: MovesToWorkloadIdentity, Retires, OnIslandList, HandedOff or Unreconciled. When the program confirms or revises D11 (D09, week 36), end-state.json changes in a reviewed pull request and the run is repeated inside the 72-day margin before G5.`,
