      detail: `You need PowerShell 7.1 or later with Pester 5. Work in examples/non-person-identity, with Chapter 01's out/inventory in place (Lab 1 of Chapter 01, step 3). Step 1, run Learn's procedures against the stand-ins: Invoke-Pester -Path tests/KerberosIslandSamples.Tests.ps1 -Output None -PassThru | Select-Object PassedCount, FailedCount, NotRunCount gives PassedCount 17, FailedCount 0, NotRunCount 0. Read the test for the state-3 step: Learn's block fails with "A parameter cannot be found that matches parameter name 'Properties'". Step 2, list what each task runs: kerberos-island: Get-ADComputer, Get-ADDomainController, Get-ADObject, Get-ADServiceAccount, Get-ADUser. kerberos-apply: Complete-ADServiceAccountMigration, Disable-ADAccount, Get-ADComputer, Get-ADDomainController, Get-ADObject, Get-ADServiceAccount, Get-ADUser, New-ADServiceAccount, Set-ADServiceAccount, Start-ADServiceAccountMigration. Step 3, check the Kerberos accounts and build the plan: ./Invoke-NpiKerberosIsland.ps1 -Cloud gcc -RegisterRun out/inventory -FixturePath tests/fixtures/estate.json -KerberosFixturePath tests/fixtures/ch06/ad-kerberos.json -InputPath tests/fixtures/ch06/inputs -OutputPath out/kerberos. Output: Kerberos accounts: 9 in scope; KDS root key Ready. Findings: 6 Finding, 1 Warn, 2 Info. Plan: 9 actions, 4 of them writes (1 CompleteDmsaMigration, 2 CreateGmsa, 1 SetRetrievers); nothing sent. Island list: 5 accounts, 3 ready for P4.6; hand-off ready: False. Reconciliation (D11 KerberosIsland): 1 HandedOff, 1 MovesToWorkloadIdentity, 3 OnIslandList, 1 Unreconciled. Plan SHA-256: 5e1f7c33491948026603746e933fafed0572fb77532ff1477ad452397c353746. The plan's hash is the same on every run with these inputs. The commands run Learn's pinned procedures against stand-ins, and run the example against a fictional estate and a fake Active Directory; -Apply in Lab 1 changes only the fake, in memory.`,
