      say: `Reading the findings is where the rules become concrete. One web server account is trusted for unconstrained delegation, which stops working after a delegated migration, so that conversion is blocked. Another account's reviewed retrievers add a server that Active Directory doesn't have yet, and its end date runs past the program's deadline. An intranet account has no owner and an end date years out, so it can't be reconciled. One sits in Domain Admins. Meanwhile the plan completes a migration that started forty days ago, and creates two new group accounts.`,
      detail: `Step 4, read the findings: Get-Content out/kerberos/findings.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json | Sort-Object Rule | Format-Table Rule, Severity, ObjectKey. NPI-KRB-03 Finding gmsa-web$; NPI-KRB-04 Finding svc-webfront; NPI-KRB-05 Finding svc-intranet; NPI-KRB-06 Finding gmsa-web$; NPI-KRB-06 Finding svc-intranet; NPI-KRB-07 Finding gmsa-intranet$; NPI-KRB-08 Warn gmsa-ops$; NPI-KRB-09 Info gmsa-sql$; NPI-KRB-09 Info svc-sqlprod. svc-webfront is trusted for unconstrained delegation, which stops working once a dMSA migration completes, so its dMSA is blocked. gmsa-web$'s reviewed retrievers add WEB03, and its end date (September 30, 2027) is after D08's (June 30, 2027). svc-intranet has no SPN owner, and its end date (2028) is after D08 and after the island's end of life, so its planned gMSA isn't reconciled. gmsa-ops$ is in Domain Admins. Step 5, read the plan: MovesToWorkloadIdentity gmsa-ops$ (no write); HandedOff gmsa-sql$; Island gmsa-web$; SetRetrievers gmsa-web$ (write, Set-ADServiceAccount); CreateGmsa msa-print01$ (write, New-ADServiceAccount); CompleteDmsaMigration svc-hrsync (write, Complete-ADServiceAccountMigration); CreateGmsa svc-intranet (write, New-ADServiceAccount); HandedOff svc-sqlprod; Blocked svc-webfront. svc-hrsync's migration to dmsa-hrsync$ started on September 20, 40 days ago, so it can complete. The MSA msa-print01$ gets a new gMSA for its scheduled task; the IIS application pool's account svc-intranet gets one whose retrievers are a group.`,
