      detail: `Checklist: every Kerberos account in the register has a reviewed disposition, or a finding with an owner of the fix. The KDS root key check ran with a delegated read of the start time only, not as a Domain Admin. Every gMSA's and dMSA's retrievers match password-retrievers.json. No dMSA was planned for an MSA, an account with unconstrained delegation, or a host without Windows Server 2025, and none was completed before 28 days. Every plan's SHA-256 was approved by someone other than the person who applied it, and the write path's manifest is filed with the change record. No old account was deleted; each superseded one is disabled and has a retirement decision. Every account on the island list has an SPN owner and an end date within D08, and the list went to the program's SPN retirement (P4.6) only when islandHandoffReady was true. Every gMSA and dMSA is MovesToWorkloadIdentity, Retires, OnIslandList or HandedOff against the current end-state.json, and the run was repeated after D11 was confirmed. The pinned Learn pages match their manifest, and every upstream commit since the pin has been reviewed. Next: Chapter 07 — Least Privilege for Service Principals.`,
